+TASK
+
+Goal:
+Make the app shell's asset references absolute under `/app/` so they resolve correctly no
+matter which URL form loaded the document.
+
+Relevant Requirements:
+Correction for the third finding (OPTIONAL) in `.harness/reviews/M10-cycle1.md`
+("`https://<host>/app` without a trailing slash serves `index.html` at path `/app`, where
+the shell's relative `href`s resolve to the origin root and 404/401"). Read that finding in
+the report. Do not read the rest of the report.
+
+Acceptance Criteria:
+- `web/public/index.html`'s three asset references become absolute, `/app/`-rooted paths,
+  matching the convention `web/public/app.webmanifest` already uses for its icons
+  (`/app/icons/icon-192.png` etc.):
+  - line 20 `href="./app.webmanifest"`        -> `href="/app/app.webmanifest"`
+  - line 21 `href="./icons/apple-touch-icon-180.png"` -> `href="/app/icons/apple-touch-icon-180.png"`
+  - line 30 `src="./main.js"`                 -> `src="/app/main.js"`
+  Change nothing else in that file. In particular do not touch the viewport meta, the
+  inline `<style>`, or any of the `apple-mobile-web-app-*` meta tags.
+- `test/web/manifest.test.ts` currently asserts the three RELATIVE forms verbatim, at
+  roughly lines 97, 104 and 122. Update those three assertions to the new absolute forms.
+  This is a convention change, not a loosening: do not delete the assertions, do not replace
+  an exact-string assertion with a weaker `toContain` of a shorter substring, and keep each
+  test's name and structure. Every other assertion in that file stays exactly as it is.
+- Add ONE new test to `test/web/manifest.test.ts` that would have caught the original bug:
+  read `web/public/index.html` and assert it contains NO `href="./` and NO `src="./`
+  occurrences at all. Confirm it discriminates by running it against the UNCHANGED
+  `index.html` first and observing it fail, then making the change. Paste that red output in
+  your Summary.
+- Do not change `src/host/pwa-server.ts`. The report offers a server-side 301 redirect as an
+  alternative correction; that alternative is explicitly NOT being taken, because
+  `stripMountPrefix` is pre-existing C4 code this milestone did not author and changing the
+  server's routing is a wider blast radius than this OPTIONAL finding warrants. This decision
+  is made — do not revisit it.
+- `~/.bun/bin/bun test` passes with no fewer tests than before, and `~/.bun/bin/bunx tsc
+  --noEmit` exits 0. Note that `test/build.test.ts` asserts `web/dist/index.html` is a byte
+  copy of `web/public/index.html`; check whether it reads from a freshly-built dist or a
+  stale one, and report in Unresolved Issues if it fails for that reason rather than
+  working around it.
+
+Relevant Files:
+- `web/public/index.html` (32 lines — read it in full)
+- `test/web/manifest.test.ts` (read it in full before editing)
+- `web/public/app.webmanifest` — read only, to confirm the absolute-path convention.
+
+Files Allowed To Change:
+- `web/public/index.html`
+- `test/web/manifest.test.ts`
+
+Constraints:
+- Follow existing repository patterns (the HTML file uses tabs).
+- Do not change unrelated behaviour.
+- Do not introduce dependencies.
+- Do not weaken tests.
+- Do NOT run `bun run build`. It rewrites `web/dist/`, which is outside your allowed files.
+  The orchestrator runs the build separately.
+- Do not run `git stash`, `git checkout --`, `git restore`, `git reset --hard` or
+  `git clean`. You share this working tree with a concurrent worker.
+
+Tests:
+`~/.bun/bin/bun test test/web/manifest.test.ts` for the red/green loop, then
+`~/.bun/bin/bun test` and `~/.bun/bin/bunx tsc --noEmit` before returning.
+Bun is NOT on PATH in non-interactive shells: use `~/.bun/bin/bun` or first
+`export PATH="$HOME/.bun/bin:$PATH"`. Node is not installed.
+
+Tier: Cheap. Routing reason: none — the exact three lines and their exact replacements are
+named, the blast radius is one HTML file and one test file, and `bun test` settles it.
+
+Return:
+- Summary (MUST include the red output from before the change)
+- Files changed
+- Tests run
+- Test result (pass/fail counts for the full suite)
+- Unresolved issues
