+TASK
+
+Goal:
+Stop `test/icons.test.ts` from writing generated icons into the repository's own source
+tree, and make it actually test the property it claims to test — that the checked-in
+`web/public/icons/*.png` are what the generator produces.
+
+Relevant Requirements:
+Correction for an OPTIONAL finding in `.harness/reviews/M10-cycle1.md` (fourth finding,
+"`test/icons.test.ts` calls `generateIcons()` with no `root`"). Read that finding in the
+report; it states the problem, the evidence and the suggested correction. Do not read the
+rest of the report.
+
+Acceptance Criteria:
+- Neither call to `generateIcons()` in `test/icons.test.ts` runs unrooted. Both pass an
+  explicit `{ root: <temp dir> }`. `scripts/generate-icons.ts:213-219` shows `root`
+  defaults to the repository when omitted — that default is what must no longer be hit
+  from the test suite.
+- Running `bun test` no longer modifies any file under `web/public/icons/`. Prove this:
+  record the three PNGs' mtimes and sha256 before a full `bun test`, and again after, and
+  show they are unchanged. Put that before/after evidence in your Summary. This is the
+  primary acceptance check and it must be demonstrated, not asserted.
+- The suite gains a real drift check: a test that reads the checked-in
+  `web/public/icons/*.png` bytes and asserts they equal bytes freshly generated into a
+  temp root, for all three icons. This test must be capable of failing — verify by
+  temporarily perturbing one checked-in PNG byte (or the freshly-generated comparison
+  buffer) in your working copy, observing the test fail, then restoring it. Report both
+  the failing and passing output. A test that cannot fail is the failure mode here.
+- Every temp dir the test creates is removed in a `finally`, following the pattern already
+  used by the existing "should generate deterministic icons" test at the end of the file.
+- No existing assertion is deleted or loosened. The existing PNG structural checks (chunk
+  walk, per-chunk CRC32, IHDR fields, IDAT inflate size, determinism) all remain and still
+  run — just against a temp root instead of the repository.
+- `web/public/icons/*.png` are NOT regenerated, rewritten or touched by you. If your work
+  accidentally rewrites them, restore them with `git`-free means is impossible (they are
+  untracked) — so simply do not run the generator against the default root at any point.
+
+Relevant Files:
+- `test/icons.test.ts` — the file to change. Two unrooted `generateIcons()` calls, around
+  lines 41 and 207.
+- `scripts/generate-icons.ts` — read `generateIcons`'s signature and its `root`/`outdir`
+  handling only. Do not change it.
+- `web/public/icons/icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png`, `apple-touch-icon-180.png` — read-only
+  inputs to the new drift check.
+
+Files Allowed To Change:
+- `test/icons.test.ts`
+
+Constraints:
+- Follow existing repository patterns (the file uses tabs; match it).
+- Do not change unrelated behaviour.
+- Do not introduce dependencies.
+- Do not weaken tests.
+- Do not modify `scripts/generate-icons.ts`. If you believe the generator needs a change to
+  make this possible, stop and report it under Unresolved Issues instead.
+- Do not run `git stash`, `git checkout --`, `git restore`, `git reset --hard` or
+  `git clean`. You share this working tree.
+
+Tests:
+`~/.bun/bin/bun test test/icons.test.ts` for the focused loop, then the full
+`~/.bun/bin/bun test` for the mtime/sha256 before-and-after evidence.
+Bun is NOT on PATH in non-interactive shells: use `~/.bun/bin/bun` or first
+`export PATH="$HOME/.bun/bin:$PATH"`. Node is not installed.
+
+Tier: Cheap. Routing reason: none — clearly specified, bounded to one test file, low risk
+(test-only), and settled by a command.
+
+Return:
+- Summary (including the mtime/sha256 before-and-after evidence and the deliberate-failure
+  evidence for the new drift check)
+- Files changed
+- Tests run
+- Test result
+- Unresolved issues
